OrionLayer open fix 66 — the battle's scan view and board popup on the wire
===========================================================================

Work order 199 (Part C, step C1). orion2re 121950ed on `orionlayer-local`, on
top of 9e19c9f3 (open fix 64). src/ext only.

WHAT IS MISSING. Open fix 52 reports the battle's scan view as 66 and its
board popup as 67, but nothing said what they show. The scan view draws
MOX::_global_combat_data, the copy of the unit Display_Combat_View_Ship_
took, and keeps its index in _ship_data_id (cmbtdrw1.cpp:1549-1551); the
board popup keeps its message, its range and the marines chosen in
CMBTDRW1::_g_msg, _g_min, _g_max and _g_var (cmbtdrw1.cpp:1581-1666). None
of it was on the wire, so a client could not draw either, nor see the
effect of the popup's arrows.

WHAT THE PATCH ADDS. Snapshot section 25, "CPOP", after CMEV, written only
while a battle is live and the screen is 66 or 67: a version byte, then
int16 the screen, the battle's serial, the scanned unit (-1 in the popup),
the popup's min, max and chosen value (0 in the scan view), then a length
byte and the popup's message (empty in the scan view).

BEHAVIOUR WITHOUT ORIONLAYER: unchanged. The block is read only; nothing
in the game changes, and nothing is written outside those two screens.

HOW TO REVERT. git revert 121950ed.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 4397e198..8a9a27ce 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1702,6 +1702,37 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         }
         g_combat_event_sent = g_combat_event_next;
     }
+
+    // 25. The battle's scan view and board popup: "CPOP", written ONLY while
+    //     one of them is up in a battle (66 or 67, open fix 52's ids), after
+    //     CMEV. OrionLayer, open fix 66.
+    //
+    //     The scan view draws MOX::_global_combat_data, the copy of the unit
+    //     Display_Combat_View_Ship_ took (cmbtdrw1.cpp:1549-1551), and keeps
+    //     its index in _ship_data_id; the board popup keeps its message, its
+    //     range and the chosen marines in CMBTDRW1's _g_msg/_g_min/_g_max/
+    //     _g_var (cmbtdrw1.cpp:1581-1666). None of it was on the wire, so a
+    //     client could not say which unit is scanned, nor show the popup, nor
+    //     see the effect of an arrow. Read only; nothing here changes the game.
+    if (g_combat_live &&
+        (current_screen == SCREEN_EXT_COMBAT_SCAN || current_screen == SCREEN_EXT_COMBAT_BOARD)) {
+        const bool board = current_screen == SCREEN_EXT_COMBAT_BOARD;
+        const char* msg = (board && CMBTDRW1::_g_msg != nullptr) ? CMBTDRW1::_g_msg : "";
+        const size_t len = strnlen(msg, 255);
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'C');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'P');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'O');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'P');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, current_screen);
+        Write16(buf, (int16_t)g_combat_serial);
+        Write16(buf, board ? (int16_t)-1 : MOX::_ship_data_id);
+        Write16(buf, board ? CMBTDRW1::_g_min : (int16_t)0);
+        Write16(buf, board ? CMBTDRW1::_g_max : (int16_t)0);
+        Write16(buf, board ? CMBTDRW1::_g_var : (int16_t)0);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)len);
+        buf.insert(buf.end(), msg, msg + len);
+    }
 }
 
